2:T733,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a new kitchen renovation cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a new kitchen renovation may typically cost £8,000–£15,000 at the simpler end, £15,000–£30,000 for a mid-range project, or £30,000-plus for a larger premium renovation. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the most expensive part of a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cabinets, worktops, appliances and installation can make up a substantial part of the cost. Structural changes, moving services and premium materials can increase the budget further."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I reduce the cost of a new kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping the existing layout, retaining suitable appliances, choosing standard cabinet sizes and comparing itemised quotations can help control costs. Do not reduce the budget by overlooking necessary electrical, plumbing or preparation work."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a kitchen renovation quote include appliances and fitting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always. Ask whether the quotation includes appliances, delivery, installation, connections, old-kitchen removal, waste disposal, VAT, tiling, flooring and decorating before comparing prices."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much contingency should I allow for a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Consider allowing a contingency for unexpected work, particularly where the condition of the room is uncertain. The appropriate amount depends on the age and condition of the room and the extent of the renovation."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-is-a-new-kitchen-renovation","d"]
