pym",{"d":"M8 2v4"}],["$","path","4m81vk",{"d":"M16 2v4"}],["$","rect","1hopcy",{"width":"18","height":"18","x":"3","y":"4","rx":"2"}],["$","path","8toen8",{"d":"M3 10h18"}],"$undefined"]}],"4 August 2026",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/25","children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"BMB Renovation"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-14 sm:py-20 flex-grow bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["If you are asking how much a new kitchen renovation costs, the honest answer is that the price can vary considerably. As a rough UK guide, a straightforward replacement kitchen may typically cost around £8,000 to £15,000, while a mid-range renovation may typically fall between £15,000 and £30,000. A larger or higher-specification project, particularly one involving structural work or premium appliances, may cost more than £30,000. These are guide prices rather than fixed quotes: the room size, materials, layout and amount of building work will affect the final figure. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Typical new kitchen renovation costs"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["For budgeting purposes, it helps to divide the project into three broad levels. A basic renovation might involve standard-sized cabinets, laminate worktops, a limited number of new appliances and minimal changes to the existing plumbing and electrics. A mid-range kitchen could include made-to-measure elements, higher-specification worktops, integrated appliances, improved lighting and some plastering or flooring. A premium renovation may involve bespoke cabinetry, stone or sintered-stone worktops, a completely new layout, structural alterations and more expensive appliances."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Basic kitchen renovation: as a rough guide, typically £8,000–£15,000, depending on the room and specification."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Mid-range kitchen renovation: as a rough guide, typically £15,000–£30,000, including more extensive fitting and higher-specification finishes."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Large or premium renovation: typically £30,000 and upwards, particularly where walls, windows, services or high-end materials are involved."]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Thinking about your own project?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation covers Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead and beyond — all trades in-house. Call +44 7775 758 717 or send us a message."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get a Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"What is included in the cost?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["The largest parts of the budget can include cabinets, worktops, appliances and labour. Cabinet prices depend on the number of units, storage accessories, door style and whether the units are flat-pack, rigid or bespoke. As a rough guide, cabinets may account for around £3,000–£12,000 or more. Worktops may range from around £500 for a simple laminate option to several thousand pounds for natural stone, quartz or other premium surfaces. The exact amount depends on the length, cut-outs, edging and installation requirements. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Cabinets and storage: as a rough guide, approximately £3,000–£12,000-plus."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Worktops: as a rough guide, approximately £500–£5,000-plus, depending on the material and design."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Appliances: typically approximately £2,000–£10,000 for a full set, although keeping suitable existing appliances can reduce the total."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Installation and associated trades: this may cost several thousand pounds, depending on the complexity and duration of the work."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Common extras that can change the budget"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A kitchen quotation may look affordable until associated work is included. Moving a sink, dishwasher, cooker or radiator can require changes to plumbing, electrics or gas arrangements. Removing a wall, widening a doorway or installing a roof lantern can add structural and design costs. Other possible extras include plastering, painting, new flooring, splashbacks, tiling, lighting, extractor installation, waste removal and making good after the old kitchen is removed."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Allow for the less visible work"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Before comparing prices, check whether the quotation includes dismantling and disposal of the existing kitchen, preparation of walls and floors, fitting of appliances, electrical alterations, plumbing, tiling and final connections. Also ask whether VAT is included. If the old room reveals damaged plaster, uneven floors, outdated wiring or leaking pipework, remedial work may be necessary before the new units can be installed. Consider setting aside a contingency for unexpected work, but discuss an appropriate allowance with your contractor because the amount will vary by project."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"How to plan a more accurate kitchen budget"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Start with a measured plan rather than choosing products at random. Record the room dimensions, window and door positions, ceiling height, existing service locations and any appliances you intend to retain. Then decide which elements matter most to you. For example, you may prefer to spend more on durable worktops and storage while choosing standard cabinet doors, or invest in appliances while keeping the existing layout. Keeping plumbing and electrical points in broadly the same positions can reduce the amount of alteration work needed, although suitability should be checked on site."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Create a complete list of cabinets, panels, handles, worktops, appliances and accessories before requesting prices."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Ask for labour, delivery, disposal, preparation, VAT and finishing work to be shown separately."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Confirm who is responsible for appliance connections, tiling, flooring, decorating and waste removal."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Obtain comparable written quotations based on the same specification, not just similar-looking cabinet prices."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Keep a contingency for hidden defects and choose appliances and finishes before the final order is placed."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Getting a kitchen renovation quote in Hertfordshire and nearby areas"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["For homeowners in Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead, Borehamwood, Harrow, Croxley Green, Luton or Bedford, a site visit can help turn a broad estimate into a more useful budget. BMB Renovation is based at 157 Judge Street, Watford WD24 5AN, and offers kitchen fitting and renovation. All plumbing, tiling, electrical and cabinet installation work is handled in-house. You can review ",["$","$L4","0",{"href":"/kitchen-fitting-watford","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"kitchen fitting in Watford"}],", see the wider ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/services","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"renovation services"}],", or request a ",["$","$L4","2",{"href":"/contact","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"free, no-obligation quote"}],"."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Questions to ask before accepting a quotation"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Ask whether the quote is based on a fixed design and specification, and what happens if you change a product after ordering. Check the expected start date, project duration, payment stages, protection of adjoining rooms and arrangements for water, cooking and refrigeration while the work is under way. A detailed quote should make clear what is included and excluded, so you can compare the full scope of each option rather than choosing the lowest headline figure. Every kitchen is different, so a measured survey and itemised quotation are generally more useful than a generic online calculator."]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Get a Free, No-Obligation Quote"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation handles kitchens, bathrooms and full home renovations across Watford, Hertfordshire, North London & Bedfordshire — all trades in-house. Tell us about your project today."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get My Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4","children":[["